# ARS (Academic Research Sharing) Platform — Engineering Rules

## 1. Technology Stack & Environment

- **Frontend:** React, TypeScript, Vite, CSS Modules, Axios (`ARS_FE`)
- **Backend:** RESTful API (.NET Core)
- **Database:** MySQL (Relational metadata, user accounts, transactions)
- **File Storage:** Firebase Cloud Storage (PDF uploads for manuscripts, verification dossiers, assignments)
- **API URL Base:** ALWAYS use `import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL`. NEVER hardcode `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, or explicit port numbers in source code.

## 2. Design System & Tokens (Figma Alignment)

- **Header Background:** `#2D3561` (Dark Navy)
- **Sidebar Background:** `#323964` (Dark Navy)
- **Main Canvas Background:** `#F8FAFC` (Light Grey)
- **Primary Accent / Buttons:** `#007AFF` (Bright Blue)
- **Icons:** Single-color monochrome line icons (`#A0AEC0`)
- **Styling Method:** Standardize on CSS Modules or Tailwind CSS utility classes. Avoid inline style objects.

## 3. User Roles & Governance

| Role | Type | Upgrade Proof / Action | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **System Admin** | Fixed | System management | Payout clearance, user moderation, audit log CSV exports |
| **Lecturer** | Acquirable | Teaching License PDF | Group creation, student supervision, seminar Google Meet links |
| **Researcher** | Acquirable | Research focus notes | Manuscript submission, review tracking, paper revisions |
| **Reviewer** | Acquirable | DOI link or Paper PDF | Peer evaluation, feedback submission, wallet balance & withdrawals |
| **Graduate Student** | Base Tier | Fixed assignment | Cannot request upgrades; others cannot downgrade to it |

## 4. Auth & Role Switching Mechanics

- **Authentication:** Custom backend JWT managed in MySQL (No Firebase Auth).
- **Email Verification:** SMTP tokens stored in MySQL (`is_email_verified`, `verification_token`).
- **Dynamic Role Switching:** Header workspace selection MUST call `POST /api/auth/switch-role` to update JWT claims without forcing user logout.

## 5. Core Architectural & Code Rules

- **No Mock Data:** Components MUST fetch live dynamic data from API endpoints. Do not fall back to static arrays unless explicit fallback props are requested.
- **Firebase PDF Flow:** Frontend uploads binary PDF directly to Firebase Cloud Storage, then sends returned public URL (`pdfUrl`) to the .NET backend endpoint.
- **Withdrawal Schema Fields:** `WithdrawalRequestId`, `UserId`, `WalletId`, `BankName`, `AccountNumber`, `AccountName`, `Amount`, `Status`, `Note`, `RejectionReason`, `CreatedAt`, `UpdatedAt`.
